================================================================================
1.1 MICRO-CENT FRICTION LIMIT ($50 -> 5000 cents)
================================================================================
Capital: $50.0 = 5000.0 cents
Target risk: 1.0% = $0.5 = 50.0 cents
Min lot 0.01 => pip value $0.1 = 10.0 cents

SL (pips)  Risk $ (0.01 lot)  Risk % $50   Risk cents   Risk % 5000c  Min lot for 1%   Bal needed 1%  
20         $2.00              4.00       % 200          4.00        % 0.00250          $200           
40         $4.00              8.00       % 400          8.00        % 0.00125          $400           
60         $6.00              12.00      % 600          12.00       % 0.00083          $600           
88         $8.80              17.60      % 880          17.60       % 0.00057          $880           

ANALYSIS:
- For SL=20 pips, min risk = $2.00 = 4% of $50 capital -> violates 1% rule by 4x
- For SL=88 pips (2.2 ATR cap), min risk = $8.80 = 17.6% of capital -> catastrophic over-leverage
- Required balance to maintain 1% risk at 0.01 lot:
  SL 20 pips -> $200 minimum
  SL 40 pips -> $400 minimum
  SL 60 pips -> $600 minimum
  SL 88 pips -> $880 minimum
- In cent account, same math holds: 20 pips = 200 cents = 4% of 5000c
- Broker constraint: cannot go below 0.01 lot on standard cent. Need broker offering 0.001 lot (0.1 cent lots) or nano lots.
- Structural solution: capital must be >= $200 for 20-pip SL, >= $880 for 88-pip SL to respect 1% rule at 0.01 lot.
- If using 0.001 lot brokers (pip value $0.01), $50 can support 1% risk up to 50 pips SL.

