Tipping point where E[R] gross becomes negative: spread ~ None pips (total friction ~ N/A pips)
Exact breakeven spread (gross edge 0.095R): 5.39 pips (total 5.74 pips)
Exact breakeven spread (net edge 0.02R): 0.85 pips (total 1.20 pips)

Friction Ratio = (Spread+Commission)/SL
For SL=60 pips, Friction Ratio at 0.5 pip spread = 1.42%
For SL=20 pips tight SL, Friction Ratio at 0.5 pip = 4.25% -> much worse for tight stops
Task's threshold: Friction Ratio exceeds 15% of expectancy
15% of E[R]_gross (0.095R) = 0.0144R = 0.86 pips
15% of E[R]_net (0.02R) = 0.0030R = 0.18 pips
=> Even 0.5 pip spread destroys >15% of net edge if net edge only 0.02R, because 0.85 pips total =0.014R which is 70% of 0.02R

